Cell["5. Mechanism: a background-parity confound", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dcc348d3-1216-42a8-9f9a-63008842023c"],

Cell["\<\
Odd rule numbers have f(0,0,0)=1: the seed evolves on a blinking background, \
so massDimension (cells differing from background) sees only a linearly \
growing deviation, giving D~1. Of the 35 chaotic-yet-low-D rules, 32 are odd; \
all 16 high-D chaotic rules are even. Class-3 mean D: 1.66 (even) vs 1.01 \
(odd). Genuine even-background outliers: 106, 120, 184.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"afcef4fb-7adf-4a39-92f6-be613ca0c79f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"even-bg mean D\"\>", "\[Rule]", "1.6600000000000001`"}], ",", 
   
   RowBox[{"\<\"odd-bg mean D\"\>", "\[Rule]", "1.01`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"genuine even outliers\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"106", ",", "120", ",", "184"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",Expr\
essionUUID->"19f45d3d-f662-4bf7-9c60-4f8da72c22dd"],

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5e6b5301-335a-46b9-bb93-b3636816a685"],

Cell["\<\
Single-seed mass dimension is not a usable proxy for Wolfram class. It \
collapses order (class 2) and chaos (class 3) onto D~1, lets a trivial rule \
(254) hold the maximal dimension, and much of its faint residual correlation \
is a background-parity artifact rather than dynamics. Verified over all 256 \
rules; class labels are a proxy validated on 27 anchors. See findings.md for \
full epistemics and refutation log.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00c5c6be-1ec4-4c6f-b07c-1965dd71c37d"]
},
